From: 181981772 <181981772@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: dpcm: replay deferred routes after FE recovery

Do not let a DAPM route update tear down a DPCM backend retained after a
failed FE hw_free. Remember deferred route changes and replay the current
DAPM paths after FE reconfiguration succeeds or close disconnects the FE.
Propagate DPCM startup, shutdown, and route-connect errors so partial
updates stay pending until a complete retry succeeds.

Track changes made by each path-add operation. If a later connection fails,
remove only links allocated by that operation and restore retained links to
their previous update and backend state. A retained BE restarted while the
path is reactivated is stopped again during rollback. If that STOP fails,
the link and running BE stay attached and the route update remains pending
for a later full retry. Ordinary PCM STOP retains its existing best-effort
behavior.

Keep links updated by a failed startup attached with their runtime-update
state intact so the next full route pass can finish the transaction. A BE
left CLOSE or NEW by that failed startup is reopened when its retained
link is reused. Propagate path-add failures from normal and compressed PCM
opens.

Record when a route-update STOP has already handled a link's running
reference. A retry then converges the exact old link before reconnecting it
from the current DAPM graph instead of decrementing a shared backend again.
On retry, force every retained old link through the normal shutdown path so
a graph change back to its previous shape cannot skip pending cleanup.

Signed-off-by: 181981772 <181981772@qq.com>

---

